  "implementation": {
    "termux_0009": "Exact clipped regions are atomically split into 16-rectangle entries. All chunks share one Present serial and ownership fence. Queue capacity remains 8 entries (128 rectangles maximum).",
    "termux_0010": "AHB root is mapped only for actual CPU access. CPU cache flush finishes before releasing the GPU ownership mutex; GPU-only frames avoid whole-screen CPU lock/unlock.",
    "termux_0011": "CPU access also waits for the already-published GPU serial watermark, releasing the renderer mutex while waiting. Does not wait for main-thread Ack counters; disconnect/timeout refuses unsafe access.",
    "wsi_0012": "At most two requests reserve distinct consecutive MSC targets after one-request epoch bootstrap. Only Complete releases pacing credit, not Idle. Older Complete cannot overwrite a future reservation. Legacy/lower-cap timer behavior, SKIP recovery, cancellation and GPU ownership fences remain."
  },
